# Resources/ is game content, not build output - never ignore anything under it.
#
# The parent .gitignore (Games/.gitignore:77) has `*.obj`, the Visual Studio rule for
# compiled object files. That pattern also matches the entity 3D *models* under
# Resources/Entities/, which is why none of them were ever committed. This negation is
# last and lives in a nested .gitignore, so it overrides both the rules above and the
# parent's - without un-ignoring real build output in your other projects.
!Resources/**
